#
# Four subjects carrying {10, 20, 20, 30} — the repeated value (20) is
# DELIBERATELY neither the minimum (10) nor the maximum (30) nor the first
# (m1 = 10) nor the last (m4 = 30) row, so this fixture can only pass for the
# right reason: MODE finding the genuinely repeated value discriminates from
# every coincidental stand-in (MIN, MAX, FIRST, LAST) an incorrect
# implementation could fall back to and still pass an all-distinct or
# smallest-repeats-first tie-break dataset.
@prefix : <https://example.org/agg-stat#> .

:m1 :value 10 .
:m2 :value 20 .
:m3 :value 20 .
:m4 :value 30 .
